  "$comment": "Settings structure (ADR 0112 in bipe/docs/adr). One source for the order of groups, sections and rows on iOS and Android. `root` is the order of the group rows under Configurações in the Você tab; `profile` opens from the Você header. A group with `screen: \"element\"` keeps the Element screen and lists no rows here. Row kinds: link (opens a screen), choice (opens a picker), switch, info (a value, no action), url (opens a page from `urls`), action (runs something), destructive. `gate`: absent = always shown; `ios` or `android` = that platform only; `flag:<name>` = behind that app feature flag; `planned:<issue>` = hidden until bipe-chat/bipe#<issue> ships. Titles are bipe_* string keys; a row without its own string has no place here. A new top-level group needs a new ADR.",
